{"overview":"Sergei’s beloved wife Yelena has passed away, and the bereaved husband is inconsolable. He remains obsessed with pictures of Yelena and with a braid of her hair that he has saved. One day, while walking in the street, he passes by a woman who bears a striking resemblance to Yelena.","cast":[{"n":"Alexander Wyrubow","c":"Sergei Nikolaevich Nedelin","p":"/kSZ1AD02aHVFtVHCr8rawArhEEK.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Elena Verkhovetskaya","c":"Elena, his wife","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Nina Tschernobajewa","c":"Tina Wiarskaya, opera singer","p":"/ofU9TBQDgBWVhMdLHzYG3dcmtdV.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Viktor Arens","c":"Solski, Nedelin's friend","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Alexandr Vyrubov","c":"","p":null,"q":"Q18237738"}],"country":["Russian Empire"],"language":["Russian"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daydreams_(1915_film)","qid":"Q17492300","rel":{"RU":{"d":"1915-10-10"}},"backdrops":["/V2VgspdvahVMIqRH5LrZCsny9g.jpg","/cLaai3frl6OhdUtMNSBT7MLWSC3.jpg","/9CqSLnecA7mHC9bhHtlkeSEjkOJ.jpg","/mTLl6FHAEVWXnUMbBrZFZ6IFuzJ.jpg"]}